From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 16:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] iommu/sun50i: Advertise the page sizes map and unmap handle

Map and unmap write a run of 4 KiB entries in one call, but the domain
still advertises 4 KiB alone, so the IOMMU core maps a buffer one page at
a time, each call flushing a single entry: importing a 25 MB 4K frame
costs about 4.4 ms, and as much again to unmap it. Advertise every size
from 4 KiB to 1 MiB, the span of one page table.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>

---
 drivers/iommu/sun50i-iommu.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/iommu/sun50i-iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/sun50i-iommu.c
@@ -725,7 +725,8 @@
 
 	refcount_set(&sun50i_domain->refcnt, 1);
 
-	sun50i_domain->domain.pgsize_bitmap = SZ_4K;
+	/* runs of 4 KiB entries within one 1 MiB page table, as map and unmap write them */
+	sun50i_domain->domain.pgsize_bitmap = GENMASK(20, 12);
 
 	sun50i_domain->domain.geometry.aperture_start = 0;
 	sun50i_domain->domain.geometry.aperture_end = DMA_BIT_MASK(32);
